# MacDisplayLinkPacer.swift — added by 0010-pace-redraws-on-display-link.patch, no
# upstream counterpart. This is the hash verify-vendor.sh requires (checked in
# verify-vendor-views.sh).
#
# What 0010 does: upstream coalesces redraws with asyncAfter(+16.67ms) from the first
# queued byte, which has no relationship to vsync. A 60fps producer is coalesced to ~30fps
# (measured 94/188 paints at 120Hz) and the surviving paints land at a drifting phase of
# the refresh (~2ms spread). The pacer drives both redraw queues from
# NSView.displayLink(target:selector:) in .common mode, pauses after 8 idle ticks, has a
# 100ms watchdog for a link that stops ticking, and rebinds on window change. Measured
# after: 188/188 paints, p50 interval 16.6ms, phase spread 0.2-0.4ms.
#
# Severity: SILENT. A tree missing 0010 builds and runs; it just paints unevenly.
# SWIFTTERM_DISPLAY_LINK=0 is the runtime kill switch back to upstream's timer, which is
# also how app/Scripts/check-display-link.sh measures the old path for its falsification
# case (the old timer must FAIL the gate's bounds, and does).
#
# Regenerate with:
#   shasum -a 256 vendor/SwiftTerm/Sources/SwiftTerm/Mac/MacDisplayLinkPacer.swift
mac_display_link_pacer = 15395368a055fb89b5caf7ca17b77a6fc2015757958f33271ae67765795bd200

# Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift AFTER 0011-cache-empty-glyphs-and-font-names.patch
# AND 0012-rasterize-color-glyphs-at-logical-size.patch (one combined hash, the Buffer.swift
# rule: a tree with only one of them matches neither), and the pristine v1.15.0 file (no
# earlier patch touches it). Checked in verify-vendor-views.sh. 0012's part is three
# hunks: GlyphKey gains backingScale, the frame sets rasterizer.backingScale beside
# fontSmoothing, and glyphEntry keys on it. See the 0012 entry below for why.
#
# What 0011 does: glyphEntry(for:glyph:) cached only successful rasterizations, and
# CoreTextGlyphRasterizer returns nil for zero-bounds glyphs (the space), so every blank
# cell of every rebuilt row re-asked CTFontGetBoundingRectsForGlyphs; the key also called
# CTFontCopyPostScriptName per glyph. A pane whose only activity is a 12 Hz agent spinner
# spent most of its row-build time there (23 of 37 sampled stacks). 0011 remembers
# ZERO-BOUNDS misses in emptyGlyphs (cleared on atlas reset) — only that nil path is
# deterministic for a given (font, size, glyph) and safe to cache permanently. The other
# three rasterize() nil paths (empty baseAddress, CGColorSpace, CGContext) fire after the
# bounds check and are NOT cached; caching them would leave a real glyph blank until the
# next atlas reset (GlyphAtlas.swift:123-165). 0011 also memoizes the name per scaled font.
#
# Severity: SILENT. A tree missing 0011 draws identically; it just burns idle CPU.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   shasum -a 256 vendor/SwiftTerm/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift
patched_metal_terminal_renderer  = f7be237b4ebd3549e22fb5353c8f1ecc391b092f3c6b14918ace84a927784666
upstream_metal_terminal_renderer = 916d4e1cb0ecf36bcb3dcd8d8b0d9cb79b2c5b5653c0f075ecce6a603133b166

# Apple/Metal/CoreTextGlyphRasterizer.swift AFTER 0012-rasterize-color-glyphs-at-logical-size.patch,
# and the pristine v1.15.0 file (no earlier patch touches it; the upstream hash was
# confirmed against the v1.15.0 raw file on GitHub). Checked in verify-vendor-views.sh,
# BEFORE the MetalTerminalRenderer.swift hash, so a tree missing 0012 is named.
#
# What 0012 fixes (N4, .afk/research/rendering-audit-2026-10-05.md): under Metal, colour
# emoji were ~20% smaller than under Core Text and sat left/low in their 2-cell slot. The
# Metal renderer rasterizes a font already scaled to DEVICE size (scaledFontFor) at 1:1.
# For outline glyphs that equals Core Text's logical size under a 2x CTM. For Apple Color
# Emoji it does not: the font picks its bitmap strike and its metrics by point size,
# non-linearly (U+1F600: 17.5pt wide at 14pt, but 28.0pt, not 35, at 28pt; drawn, 28pt@1x
# is 27x26 px of ink where 14pt@2x is 33x33). 0012 rasterizes COLOUR glyphs only at
# logical size under a scaled CTM, Core Text's own recipe; outline glyphs are untouched.
#
# Severity: VISIBLE. app/Scripts/check-render-parity.sh case (d) FAILS with 0012 reverted
# (emoji bbox 8px off, ink 0.62-0.69x) and passes with it (bbox <= 1px, ink 0.98-1.00x).
#
# Regenerate with:
#   shasum -a 256 vendor/SwiftTerm/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/Metal/CoreTextGlyphRasterizer.swift
patched_core_text_glyph_rasterizer  = fb2d4d84d983b866360f3554bb0944aa3df27f918c101090608b73dcf325aa8f
upstream_core_text_glyph_rasterizer = 004b090d29af185136598aeed372dee4ad2d5611018441b64e0e57f39723082c
